      "content": "it's not just glitches though. i literally saw a post from my sister yesterday that used a specific typo i make all the time—a weird way i use \"its\" instead of \"it's\"—and she's never even done that before. and then i saw a comment on my own old photo that sounded exactly like my internal monologue. if it's just an algorithm, why is it mimicking my specific linguistic patterns so perfectly? it feels like there's a digital copy of my personality being deployed. how would i even know if an AI has processed my data well enough to pass as me to the people who know me best?",
